# Gateway SSH entry - key-only, forwarding only. The proxy account has
# no usable shell (/bin/false in the images) and ForceCommand below
# makes every session channel run /bin/false, so neither an interactive
# shell nor a remote command can ever execute; only port forwarding
# (-D/-L/-R) is available to key holders.
# No HostKey lines here on purpose: the persistent host keys live in
# the data volume, whose filesystem may not preserve Unix permissions
# (an object-storage mount presents every file as 0777, and sshd
# refuses a private host key that others can access). Every launcher
# stages root-owned 0600 copies under /tmp and passes them explicitly
# with sshd -h, so sshd is never left to a default host-key location.
PermitRootLogin no
PasswordAuthentication no
KbdInteractiveAuthentication no
PubkeyAuthentication yes
AllowUsers proxy
AuthorizedKeysFile .ssh/authorized_keys
AllowTcpForwarding yes
ForceCommand /bin/false
GatewayPorts no
PermitTunnel no
X11Forwarding no
PrintMotd no
